  "Novelist and short-story writer; the finest American regionalist of the 1870s and the close friend of Henry James.",
  "Born Constance Fenimore Woolson at Claremont, New Hampshire, on 5 March 1840, a great-niece of James Fenimore Cooper; she grew up in Cleveland, published Castle Nowhere (1875) and Rodman the Keeper (1880), and lived in Europe from 1879. Anne (1882), For the Major (1883) and Jupiter Lights (1889) followed. She died in Venice on 24 January 1894.",
