  "Born Helen Maria Fiske at Amherst, Massachusetts, on 15 October 1830; after the deaths of her husband and two sons she turned to writing, publishing Verses (1870), Bits of Travel (1872) and Saxe Holm's Stories (1874). A Century of Dishonor (1881) and Ramona (1884) made her the leading advocate of Indian rights. She died in San Francisco on 12 August 1885.",
