  "Born in Cambridge, Massachusetts, on 22 December 1823; he was a Unitarian minister, a leading abolitionist, and the colonel of the 1st South Carolina Volunteers, the first Black regiment in the Union army. Army Life in a Black Regiment (1870), Common Sense about Women (1881) and his editions of Margaret Fuller and Emily Dickinson followed. He died in Cambridge on 9 May 1911.",
